the full trailer for season two of the  witcher has finally dropped and fans are  buzzing about the return of this beloved  series from intriguing monsters to  geralt's continued adventures here's  just a few of the small details you  might have missed in the trailer for the  witcher season 2. one of the first fight  scenes shown in the trailer for the  witcher season 2 is between girls and a  woman who's depicted emitting a  superhuman scream as it turns out that  woman is a type of vampire known as a  bruxer who are known for using their  piercing screams to send their enemies  flying since neverland also appears in  the trailer it makes sense to assume  that this brucer is varina who was  introduced in the short story a grain of  truth from the book the last wish in the  story varina and nevalin are lovers and  geralt originally thinks farina is a  nymph called a rusalka though he  realizes that she's much more dangerous  farina could also assume the form of a  giant bat which renders her even more  powerful in her fight against geralt in  the opening of the witcher season 2  trailer we hear a mysterious voice  speaking about how strange the world is  lately and there may be the various  signs for an omen signaling the end of  days gary world doesn't seem to be  concerned though it's then revealed that  geralt is speaking to neverland a ball  like man beast played by game of thrones  actor christopher hivue at about the 118  mark in the trailer we see a mage appear  with a scarred face brandishing a  powerful fire spell he shows up again in  the later half of the trailer this time  attacking an unknown foe the wizard is  rhians played by chris fulton and he is  one nasty customer in the novels riens  is a deadly assassin who is tasked with  capturing siri he is known for being  merciless and willing to do whatever it  takes to find his prey even torturing  people for information in season one we  were only given a quick glimpse of the  elves living in the world of the witcher  in the episode four marks geralt and  yaskir come across two elves angry  refugees who kidnap the pair when they  wander onto their territory the episode  reveals that the once proud race of  elves were driven from their homes and  forced into hiding thanks to humans who  committed near genocide on their people  not all of the elves have disappeared  however in the witcher season 2 trailer  we see a new character introduced a  beautiful female elf her name is  francesca finderbear and she is queen of  the elves as well as a powerful mage in  the books she joins the side of  nilfgaard in the return for the elven  city of del blasfana which she will rule  she also later joins a powerful lodge of  sorcerouses a secret group that hopes to  put sorceresses and power over all of  the continent one of the biggest  storylines in season 2 will tackle  siri's training at cair mohen the home  of the witchers although she has had a  harrowing ordeal so far geralt knows her  trials are just beginning about two  minutes into the witcher season 2  trailer we see geralt and siri facing  off against a wicked looking tree  monster fans of both the books and the  games may recognize this creature as a  leshy or leshen a forest demon who  wreaks havoc upon any who dare cross its  threshold the world of the witcher  boasts many powerful sorceresses yet  some of the most influential characters  are not skilled with magic but wisdom in  the witcher season 2 fans are introduced  to nanika in the books nanake is a  priestess of militele who has counseled  geralt many times over the years as well  as healed his battle wounds in the  trailer we see her offer some words of  wisdom to geralt about siri what you say  about that girl's power is true  you can't help her we can't say much  more without revealing big spoilers but  there's no question that nanaki knows  what dangers are in store for siri in  season 2 it looks like we'll be spending  quite a bit of time in cair moorhen the  legendary keep where witches were raised  and trained to become masterful hunters  while an assault on care morehen  resulted in most of the witches leaving  the keep we know that vesamir still  lives there and siri eventually joins  him and is trained by fellow witches  while we get several glimpses of the  grounds and outside of cair mohan in  this new trailer for season 2 we also  get a close-up of an iconic tree inside  of care morehen's great hall the tree  known as the medallion tree is adorned  with dozens of little hooks the whole  different witcher medallions which once  belonged to witchers who have since died  at the end of the witcher season 1  jennifer is attacked by fringilla vigo a  sorceress from nilfgaard and a member of  the lodge of sorceresses in the season 2  trailer we see jennifer being led in  chains by fringilla alongside other  apparent nilfgaardian prisoners in  another scene from the trailer we see  jennifer almost taunting fringilla when  she says  you're precious leaders after something  you're a pawn to get to it  like many others in the witcher series  the lodge of sorceresses has a history  of wanting to use siri for their  political gain since she's the only heir  of sintra and was born with powerful  magic it looks like siri and geralt will  have their work cut out for them if  they're going to survive season 2 of the  witcher you'll get the chance to see it  for yourself when the show arrives on  netflix december 17th  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the witcher are coming soon subscribe to  our youtube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

